# The words this repository refuses, as sha256 of the lowercased word, one per line.
# They are hashed and not written out because several of them are the very
# identifiers that must not appear in a public tree: a plaintext list of client
# names would be the leak it is meant to prevent. The readable list lives in the
# private repository, and tools/scan-identifiers.mjs hashes each word of each
# line here and compares. Hashing a short word is not secrecy, only the removal
# of a plain reading; nothing here depends on it being more than that.
